{"guide":{"questionsToConsider":["Do the reasons in the first question match the reasons your support team hears most often?","Should the survey appear inside the cancellation flow, or arrive by email right after it?","Who reads the answers from people who switched to a competitor?","Will you really write to people who leave an email, and who owns that promise?"],"howToUseResponses":"Count the reasons every month and watch which one grows. Read the follow-ups by reason, not all at once: a price complaint and a missing feature need different owners. Send the competitor answers to whoever plans the roadmap, and keep a list of emails against the problem each person named so you can write to them when it is fixed.","customizeSteps":["Edit the reasons to match your product, and add a follow-up for any new reason that deserves one.","Show the link on the cancellation confirmation page or in the confirmation email, never as a step people must complete to cancel.","Add the customer's plan as a hidden field so you can see which plans lose people and why."],"faqs":[{"q":"What should a cancellation survey ask?","a":"Start with the main reason for leaving, then ask one follow-up that fits that reason. An optional comment and a question about whether they would come back are usually all you need."},{"q":"Should a cancellation survey be required?","a":"No. Making people explain themselves before they can leave frustrates them and produces rushed answers. Keep it optional and separate from the cancellation itself."},{"q":"How long should a cancellation survey be?","a":"Short. Each person here answers the reason, one or two follow-ups and a few optional questions, because the branching skips everything that doesn't apply."},{"q":"What is the difference between a cancellation survey and a churn survey?","a":"A cancellation survey is shown at the moment someone cancels. A churn survey is often sent later, to people who stopped using the product, and can ask more about what changed."}]},"doc":{"schemaVersion":10,"title":"Cancellation survey","description":"Find out why people leave, and ask each of them the one follow-up that fits.","blocks":[{"id":"blk_cancella00","ref":"welcome","title":"Sorry to see you go. A couple of quick questions, and then you're done. Your cancellation goes ahead either way.","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"buttonLabel":"Start","type":"welcome"},{"id":"blk_cancella01","ref":"reason","title":"What's the main reason you're cancelling?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_too_expensive","label":"Too expensive","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_missing_a_feature","label":"Missing a feature I need","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_too_hard_to","label":"Too hard to use","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_found_a_better","label":"Found a better alternative","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_i_didn_t","label":"I didn't use it enough","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_no_longer_need","label":"No longer need it","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_something_else","label":"Something else","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_cancella02","ref":"price_fair","title":"What would have felt fair?","required":false,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"single_select","options":[{"id":"opt_a_lower_price","label":"A lower price for the same thing","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_a_smaller_plan","label":"A smaller plan with fewer features","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_the_price_was","label":"The price was fine, the value wasn't there","image_key":null},{"id":"opt_paying_monthly_instead","label":"Paying monthly instead of yearly, or the other way round","image_key":null}],"allowOther":false},{"id":"blk_cancella03","ref":"missing_feature","title":"Which feature were you missing?","required":true,"visibility":null,"image_key":null,"agentHints":null,"media":null,"type":"short_text","unique"